<h1>KnowledgePaat eBook Platform — Complete Manual Testing User Guide</h1>
<p><strong>Document Version:</strong> 2.0.0<br><strong>Target Environment:</strong> Staging Supabase (<code>https://lzuinimbsdxnhzmjpxmr.supabase.co</code>)<br><strong>Production Guard:</strong> STRICTLY PROTECTED (<code>csjywuflkvohytbvglxf</code> must remain untouched)<br><strong>Gateway Mode:</strong> Razorpay Test Mode Only (<code>rzp_test_...</code> — NEVER live keys or real money)<br><strong>Document Purpose:</strong> Step-by-step executable manual testing instructions for human testers operating as Administrators, Customers, and Public Visitors.</p>
<hr>
<h2>1. Quick Overview: The &quot;First Complete Journey&quot;</h2>
<p>If you are running your very first test on this platform, follow this end-to-end sanity journey (approximately 10 minutes) to confirm all core subsystems are operational before deep-diving into individual test suites:</p>
<pre><code>[1. Admin Prepares Book]
  /admin/e-books/new ──&gt; Fill metadata &amp; ₹49/₹99/₹50 pricing
  /admin/e-books/[id]/edit ──&gt; Upload cover image &amp; PDF attachment
  /admin/e-books/[id]/edit?tab=chapters ──&gt; Create chapters, mark &quot;Ready&quot;, set Chapter 1 as &quot;Free Sample&quot;
  /admin/e-books/[id]/edit?tab=publication ──&gt; Verify checklist ──&gt; Click &quot;Publish Edition to Bookstore&quot;
       │
       ▼
[2. Public Visitor Explores]
  / ──&gt; Click &quot;E-Books&quot; header button (observe smooth 350ms slide transition)
  /e-books ──&gt; Browse catalogue ──&gt; Open published book detail
  /e-books/[slug] ──&gt; Read Chapter 1 free sample without signing in ──&gt; Confirm paid chapters are locked
       │
       ▼
[3. Customer Signs In &amp; Purchases]
  /e-books/[slug] ──&gt; Select &quot;Read Online (₹49)&quot; ──&gt; Add to Cart
  /cart ──&gt; Review authoritative ₹49.00 total ──&gt; Click &quot;Proceed to Checkout&quot;
  /login?redirectTo=/checkout ──&gt; Sign in with Customer A credentials ──&gt; Lands on /checkout with cart intact
  /checkout ──&gt; Click &quot;Pay ₹49 via UPI / Cards&quot; ──&gt; Razorpay Test Mode Modal opens
  Razorpay Modal ──&gt; Enter Test Card (4100 2800 0000 1007) ──&gt; Enter OTP ──&gt; Payment verifies
  /checkout/success ──&gt; Success receipt displays ──&gt; Click &quot;Go to My Books&quot;
       │
       ▼
[4. Customer Reads &amp; Upgrades]
  /my-books ──&gt; Book card appears with &quot;Read Online&quot; badge ──&gt; Click &quot;Start Reading&quot;
  /read/[slug]/[ch1] ──&gt; Read chapter ──&gt; Scroll ──&gt; Observe &quot;Saving...&quot; then &quot;Saved&quot;
  /my-books ──&gt; Click &quot;Add PDF access — ₹50&quot; ──&gt; Complete ₹50 Test Mode upgrade payment
  /my-books ──&gt; Card elevates to &quot;Read + Download&quot; ──&gt; Click &quot;Download PDF&quot; ──&gt; PDF file downloads
       │
       ▼
[5. Administrator Audits Order]
  /admin/e-book-orders ──&gt; Locate Customer A&#39;s base order (₹49) and upgrade order (₹50)
  /admin/e-book-orders/[orderId] ──&gt; Inspect item breakdowns, payment IDs, and audit logs
</code></pre>
<hr>
<h2>2. Beginner-Friendly Setup &amp; Preconditions</h2>
<h3>2.1 Starting the Application Locally</h3>
<p>Open your terminal, navigate to the <code>frontend</code> folder, and start the local development server:</p>
<pre><code class="language-bash">cd /home/harsha/Documents/Documents/Project/KnowledgePaat/frontend

# Install dependencies if not already done
npm install

# Start local server
npm run dev
</code></pre>
<p>The application will start at <strong><code>http://localhost:3000</code></strong>.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>[!NOTE]
To test against a production-optimized build locally, execute:</p>
<pre><code class="language-bash">npm run build
npm run start
</code></pre>
</blockquote>
<h3>2.2 Confirming Staging Database Target</h3>
<p>Before clicking any buttons or entering any test data, confirm that your environment is connected <strong>only</strong> to dedicated Staging Supabase:</p>
<ol>
<li>Open <code>frontend/.env.local</code> (or review your shell environment variables).</li>
<li>Verify:<pre><code class="language-env">NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://lzuinimbsdxnhzmjpxmr.supabase.co
</code></pre>
</li>
<li><strong>CRITICAL GUARD:</strong> Confirm the project reference is <strong><code>lzuinimbsdxnhzmjpxmr</code></strong>. The production reference (<code>csjywuflkvohytbvglxf</code>) must <strong>never</strong> appear in your local configuration or test commands.</li>
</ol>
<h3>2.3 Confirming Razorpay Test Mode</h3>
<ol>
<li>In <code>frontend/.env.local</code>, inspect the Razorpay Key ID:<pre><code class="language-env">NEXT_PUBLIC_RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=rzp_test_...
</code></pre>
</li>
<li>Verify it starts with <strong><code>rzp_test_</code></strong>.</li>
<li><strong>NEVER</strong> use keys starting with <code>rzp_live_</code>. Any transaction initiated in Test Mode will not charge real money or touch live banking rails.</li>
<li>Official Razorpay Test Mode Card Documentation:<br><a href="https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/payments/test-card-details/">https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/payments/test-card-details/</a></li>
</ol>
<h3>2.4 Required Test Accounts &amp; Secure Credentials</h3>
<p>Three distinct user accounts are required for manual testing. <strong>Never store real credentials in test guides, source code, or shared transcripts.</strong> Obtain test credentials using these variable names from your secure team vault or <code>.env.local</code>:</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th align="left">Role</th>
<th align="left">Variable Name in <code>.env.local</code> / Vault</th>
<th align="left">Typical Usage in Tests</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody><tr>
<td align="left"><strong>Administrator</strong></td>
<td align="left"><code>STAGING_TEST_ADMIN_EMAIL</code><br><code>STAGING_TEST_ADMIN_PASSWORD</code></td>
<td align="left">Manages books, editions, pricing, publication, customer access grants, order ledgers, and refunds at <code>/admin/*</code>.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td align="left"><strong>Customer A</strong></td>
<td align="left"><code>STAGING_TEST_STUDENT_EMAIL</code><br><code>STAGING_TEST_STUDENT_PASSWORD</code></td>
<td align="left">Primary customer account. Purchases books, reads chapters, saves bookmarks, upgrades plans, and downloads PDFs.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td align="left"><strong>Customer B</strong></td>
<td align="left"><code>STAGING_TEST_CUSTOMER_B_EMAIL</code><br><code>STAGING_TEST_CUSTOMER_B_PASSWORD</code></td>
<td align="left">Secondary customer account. Used for multi-tenant boundary checks (confirming Customer B cannot access Customer A&#39;s books or orders).</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
<blockquote>
<p>[!TIP]
If test user accounts need provisioning or password rotation on staging, administrators can run the local helper:</p>
<pre><code class="language-bash">npx ts-node --project tsconfig.json scripts/rotate_staging_test_credentials.ts
</code></pre>
<p>This script updates staging Auth directly and places the high-entropy credentials securely into <code>frontend/.env.local</code>.</p>
</blockquote>
<h3>2.5 Browser Profiles for Independent Sessions</h3>
<p>To prevent session cookie collision between Administrator and Customers, configure three separate browser contexts:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Window 1 (Regular Browser / Profile A):</strong> Log in as <strong>Administrator</strong> at <code>http://localhost:3000/admin/login</code>.</li>
<li><strong>Window 2 (Incognito / Profile B):</strong> Log in as <strong>Customer A</strong> at <code>http://localhost:3000/login</code>.</li>
<li><strong>Window 3 (Secondary Browser, e.g., Firefox or Chrome Guest Profile):</strong> Log in as <strong>Customer B</strong> or browse anonymously as <strong>Public Visitor</strong>.</li>
</ul>
<h3>2.6 Test Assets &amp; Disposable Records Requirement</h3>
<p>Have the following test assets ready on your machine:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Cover Image:</strong> Any standard JPEG, PNG, or WebP image under 2MB (e.g., <code>500x700px</code>).</li>
<li><strong>Publication PDF:</strong> Any standard PDF document under 100MB (a sample 2-page PDF is sufficient).</li>
<li><strong>Chapter Content:</strong> Sample text formatted in Markdown (headings, paragraphs, code blocks).</li>
</ul>
<blockquote>
<p>[!IMPORTANT]
<strong>Use Disposable Records Only:</strong><br>Tests that change pricing, withdraw books from sale, revoke customer entitlements, or issue refunds must be performed on <strong>disposable staging records created during your test session</strong>. Do not alter established staging baseline books unless explicitly directed.</p>
</blockquote>
<hr>
<h2>3. Official Razorpay Test Cards Reference</h2>
<p>Use only these official Razorpay Sandbox card numbers during checkout testing. Label every entry as <strong>Test Mode</strong>:</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th align="left">Card Type</th>
<th align="left">Card Number (Test Mode Only)</th>
<th align="left">Expiry</th>
<th align="left">CVV</th>
<th align="left">Expected Result / Purpose</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody><tr>
<td align="left"><strong>Domestic Success</strong></td>
<td align="left"><code>4100 2800 0000 1007</code></td>
<td align="left">Any future date (e.g., <code>12/28</code>)</td>
<td align="left">Any 3 digits (<code>123</code>)</td>
<td align="left">Instant OTP authentication &amp; successful capture. Enter any 4- or 6-digit OTP (e.g., <code>123456</code>).</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td align="left"><strong>Alternative Success</strong></td>
<td align="left"><code>4012 0000 0000 0002</code></td>
<td align="left">Future date (<code>10/29</code>)</td>
<td align="left"><code>456</code></td>
<td align="left">Visa domestic success.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td align="left"><strong>Declined / Failed Card</strong></td>
<td align="left"><code>4000 0000 0000 1002</code></td>
<td align="left">Future date (<code>12/28</code>)</td>
<td align="left"><code>123</code></td>
<td align="left">Immediate decline by issuing bank simulation.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td align="left"><strong>Insufficient Funds</strong></td>
<td align="left"><code>4000 0000 0000 1004</code></td>
<td align="left">Future date (<code>12/28</code>)</td>
<td align="left"><code>123</code></td>
<td align="left">Simulates card failure due to insufficient credit limit.</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
<p>Official Documentation: <a href="https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/payments/test-card-details/">https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/payments/test-card-details/</a></p>
<hr>
<h2>4. Test Suite A: Administrator Prepares Books</h2>
<p>Execute this suite first to author, configure, and publish a disposable test book.</p>
<hr>
<h3>TC-ADM-01: Sign In as Administrator</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Role:</strong> Administrator</li>
<li><strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Administrator credentials available from <code>STAGING_TEST_ADMIN_EMAIL</code> and <code>STAGING_TEST_ADMIN_PASSWORD</code>.</li>
<li><strong>Starting Page:</strong> <code>http://localhost:3000/admin/login</code></li>
<li><strong>Numbered Actions:</strong><ol>
<li>Open <code>http://localhost:3000/admin/login</code> in Browser Window 1.</li>
<li>Enter the administrator email and password into the respective fields.</li>
<li>Click <strong>&quot;Sign In to Dashboard&quot;</strong>.</li>
</ol>
</li>
<li><strong>Expected Results:</strong><ul>
<li>Login succeeds without error.</li>
<li>User is redirected to <code>/admin/dashboard</code>.</li>
<li>Admin header navigation displays links to eBooks, Customers, and Orders.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><strong>Evidence to Record:</strong> Screenshot of <code>/admin/dashboard</code> showing logged-in admin state.</li>
<li><strong>Actual Result:</strong> Pending execution.</li>
<li><strong>Status:</strong> NOT RUN</li>
<li><strong>Issue Reference:</strong> None.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h3>TC-ADM-02: Create Draft Book &amp; Metadata</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Role:</strong> Administrator</li>
<li><strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Signed in as Administrator (<code>TC-ADM-01</code>).</li>
<li><strong>Starting Page:</strong> <code>http://localhost:3000/admin/e-books</code></li>
<li><strong>Numbered Actions:</strong><ol>
<li>On <code>/admin/e-books</code>, click the <strong>&quot;Add New eBook&quot;</strong> button (top right).</li>
<li>The page navigates to <code>/admin/e-books/new</code>.</li>
<li>Fill in the form fields:<ul>
<li><strong>Book Title:</strong> <code>Manual Test Guide to Cloud Architecture</code></li>
<li><strong>Author Name:</strong> <code>QA Lead Engineer</code></li>
<li><strong>URL Slug:</strong> <code>manual-test-guide-cloud-architecture</code> (auto-generated or manually typed)</li>
<li><strong>Category:</strong> <code>System Design</code></li>
<li><strong>Target Reader Role:</strong> <code>Backend Engineers &amp; Testers</code></li>
<li><strong>Subtitle:</strong> <code>A Comprehensive Hands-On Testing Guide</code></li>
<li><strong>Language:</strong> <code>en</code></li>
<li><strong>Description:</strong> <code>This disposable staging book is created specifically for manual verification of checkout, reading, downloads, and refunds.</code></li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>Review default pricing tiers shown:<ul>
<li>Online: ₹49 (4900 paise)</li>
<li>Download: ₹99 (9900 paise)</li>
<li>Upgrade: ₹50 (5000 paise)</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>Click <strong>&quot;Save &amp; Continue to Workspace&quot;</strong> (or submit button).</li>
</ol>
</li>
<li><strong>Expected Results:</strong><ul>
<li>Book record is created in <code>ebooks</code> with <code>status=&#39;draft&#39;</code>.</li>
<li>Initial Edition #1 is automatically generated in <code>ebook_editions</code>.</li>
<li>Browser automatically redirects to the editor at <code>/admin/e-books/[bookId]/edit</code>.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><strong>Evidence to Record:</strong> Note the generated <code>bookId</code> from the URL bar.</li>
<li><strong>Actual Result:</strong> Pending execution.</li>
<li><strong>Status:</strong> NOT RUN</li>
<li><strong>Issue Reference:</strong> None.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h3>TC-ADM-03: Upload Public Cover Asset</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Role:</strong> Administrator</li>
<li><strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Draft book created (<code>TC-ADM-02</code>); valid image file (<code>.jpg</code> or <code>.png</code>, &lt; 2MB).</li>
<li><strong>Starting Page:</strong> <code>/admin/e-books/[bookId]/edit?tab=details</code></li>
<li><strong>Numbered Actions:</strong><ol>
<li>On the editor page, ensure the <strong>&quot;Book Details &amp; Cover&quot;</strong> tab is active.</li>
<li>In the right-hand column under <strong>&quot;Cover Image (Public)&quot;</strong>, click the file input button (<strong>&quot;Choose File&quot;</strong>).</li>
<li>Select your test cover image.</li>
<li>Click <strong>&quot;Upload Cover&quot;</strong>.</li>
<li>After the upload finishes, click <strong>&quot;Save Book Details&quot;</strong> at the bottom of the left column.</li>
</ol>
</li>
<li><strong>Expected Results:</strong><ul>
<li>File is uploaded to the public storage bucket (<code>ebook-covers</code>).</li>
<li>Cover preview appears immediately in the preview box.</li>
<li>Green notification banner displays: <code>&quot;Cover image uploaded and attached successfully.&quot;</code></li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><strong>Evidence to Record:</strong> Screenshot showing the uploaded cover image thumbnail in the editor.</li>
<li><strong>Actual Result:</strong> Pending execution.</li>
<li><strong>Status:</strong> NOT RUN</li>
<li><strong>Issue Reference:</strong> None.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h3>TC-ADM-04: Upload Private Publication PDF to Edition</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Role:</strong> Administrator</li>
<li><strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Draft book created (<code>TC-ADM-02</code>); valid PDF document (&lt; 100MB).</li>
<li><strong>Starting Page:</strong> <code>/admin/e-books/[bookId]/edit?tab=editions</code></li>
<li><strong>Numbered Actions:</strong><ol>
<li>In the editor tab bar, click <strong>&quot;Editions &amp; PDF Files&quot;</strong>.</li>
<li>Confirm Edition #1 is selected as the active edition.</li>
<li>Under <strong>&quot;Publication PDF Document (Strictly Private)&quot;</strong>, locate the file input.</li>
<li>Select your test PDF file.</li>
<li>Click <strong>&quot;Upload PDF&quot;</strong>.</li>
</ol>
</li>
<li><strong>Expected Results:</strong><ul>
<li>File is uploaded to the private bucket (<code>ebook-pdfs</code>).</li>
<li>Storage path, original filename, and file size in MB are displayed with a green <code>&quot;Verified Attachment&quot;</code> badge.</li>
<li>Green banner confirms: <code>&quot;Publication PDF uploaded to private storage successfully.&quot;</code></li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><strong>Evidence to Record:</strong> Screenshot of the verified PDF attachment card with path and size.</li>
<li><strong>Actual Result:</strong> Pending execution.</li>
<li><strong>Status:</strong> NOT RUN</li>
<li><strong>Issue Reference:</strong> None.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h3>TC-ADM-05: Author Chapters, Mark Readiness, Reorder, &amp; Designate Free Sample</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Role:</strong> Administrator</li>
<li><strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Draft book created (<code>TC-ADM-02</code>).</li>
<li><strong>Starting Page:</strong> <code>/admin/e-books/[bookId]/edit?tab=chapters</code></li>
<li><strong>Numbered Actions:</strong><ol>
<li>Click the <strong>&quot;Website Chapters&quot;</strong> tab.</li>
<li>Click <strong>&quot;+ Add&quot;</strong> to create Chapter 1.<ul>
<li>Title: <code>Chapter 1: Cloud Architecture Fundamentals</code></li>
<li>Slug: <code>chapter-1-fundamentals</code></li>
<li>Check the box: <strong>&quot;Designate as Free Sample (Accessible to public visitors without login)&quot;</strong></li>
<li>Check the box: <strong>&quot;Ready for Publication&quot;</strong></li>
<li>Markdown Body:<pre><code class="language-markdown"># Chapter 1: Cloud Architecture Fundamentals

Welcome to the free sample chapter. This chapter is publicly accessible to all visitors.

## Key Concepts
- High availability
- Fault tolerance
- Scalable storage
</code></pre>
</li>
<li>Click <strong>&quot;Save Chapter&quot;</strong>.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>Click <strong>&quot;+ Add&quot;</strong> to create Chapter 2.<ul>
<li>Title: <code>Chapter 2: Distributed Data Stores &amp; Caching</code></li>
<li>Slug: <code>chapter-2-caching</code></li>
<li><strong>Leave &quot;Designate as Free Sample&quot; unchecked.</strong></li>
<li>Check the box: <strong>&quot;Ready for Publication&quot;</strong></li>
<li>Markdown Body:<pre><code class="language-markdown"># Chapter 2: Distributed Data Stores

This is a protected paid chapter. Only authenticated owners can read this content.
</code></pre>
</li>
<li>Click <strong>&quot;Save Chapter&quot;</strong>.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>Click the up/down chevron arrows next to Chapter 2 in the list to test reordering. Move Chapter 2 up, then move Chapter 1 back up so Chapter 1 is first.</li>
</ol>
</li>
<li><strong>Expected Results:</strong><ul>
<li>Chapter 1 shows the <code>&quot;Free Sample&quot;</code> tag and status <code>&quot;ready&quot;</code>.</li>
<li>Chapter 2 shows status <code>&quot;ready&quot;</code> without sample tag.</li>
<li>Reordering saves immediately via <code>/api/admin/ebooks/[bookId]/editions/[editionId]/chapters/reorder</code>.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><strong>Evidence to Record:</strong> Screenshot of the chapter list showing Chapter 1 (Free Sample, ready) and Chapter 2 (ready).</li>
<li><strong>Actual Result:</strong> Pending execution.</li>
<li><strong>Status:</strong> NOT RUN</li>
<li><strong>Issue Reference:</strong> None.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h3>TC-ADM-06: Configure Dynamic Commercial Pricing &amp; Discounts</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Role:</strong> Administrator</li>
<li><strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Draft book created (<code>TC-ADM-02</code>).</li>
<li><strong>Starting Page:</strong> <code>/admin/e-books/[bookId]/edit?tab=pricing</code></li>
<li><strong>Numbered Actions:</strong><ol>
<li>Click the <strong>&quot;Pricing &amp; Discounts&quot;</strong> tab.</li>
<li>Review current prices: Read Online ₹49, Read + Download ₹99, Upgrade ₹50.</li>
<li>Under <strong>Read Online Tier</strong>:<ul>
<li>Original Price: <code>49</code></li>
<li>Discount Type: <code>none</code></li>
</ul>
</li>
