<li>Open <code>/admin/e-books/[bookId]/edit?tab=pricing</code> in Tab 1.</li>
<li>Open the exact same URL in Tab 2.</li>
<li>In Tab 1: Change Read Online to <code>69</code>, enter reason <code>Tab 1 update</code>, and click <strong>&quot;Save Commercial Pricing&quot;</strong>.<ul>
<li>Verify Tab 1 saves successfully (version becomes <code>3</code>).</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>Switch to Tab 2 (which still has stale version <code>2</code> loaded in its form state).</li>
<li>In Tab 2: Change Read Online to <code>79</code>, enter reason <code>Tab 2 stale update</code>, and click <strong>&quot;Save Commercial Pricing&quot;</strong>.</li>
</ol>
</li>
<li><strong>Expected Results:</strong><ul>
<li>Tab 2 submission is intercepted by server-side optimistic concurrency control.</li>
<li>Server returns HTTP <code>409 Conflict</code>.</li>
<li>Tab 2 displays conflict banner: <code>&quot;Concurrent update conflict detected. Please reload.&quot;</code></li>
<li>Prevents accidental silent overwrites when multiple admins edit pricing simultaneously.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><strong>Evidence to Record:</strong> Screenshot of the HTTP 409 conflict error banner in Tab 2.</li>
<li><strong>Actual Result:</strong> Pending execution.</li>
<li><strong>Status:</strong> NOT RUN</li>
<li><strong>Issue Reference:</strong> None.</li>
</ul>
