<h3>TC-TECH-04: API Rate Limiting &amp; Overload Recovery</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Role:</strong> Developer / QA Engineer</li>
<li><strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Terminal access.</li>
<li><strong>Execution:</strong><ol>
<li>Run the rate limit automated verification:<pre><code class="language-bash">npx ts-node --project tsconfig.json scripts/rate_limit_worker.ts
</code></pre>
</li>
<li>Rapidly send &gt; 20 requests to <code>/api/ebooks/orders/create</code> within 60 seconds.</li>
</ol>
</li>
<li><strong>Expected Results:</strong><ul>
<li>First 20 requests succeed (or return business validation).</li>
<li>21st request returns HTTP <code>429 Too Many Requests</code>.</li>
<li>Response includes headers: <code>Retry-After: [seconds]</code> and <code>X-RateLimit-Remaining: 0</code>.</li>
<li>Database state remains completely invariant.</li>
<li>After the retry window expires, normal API requests succeed immediately.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><strong>Status:</strong> <strong>PASS</strong> (Verified in automated audit suite).</li>
<li><strong>Issue Reference:</strong> Section 8 (<code>docs/ebooks/audit-remediation-report.md</code>).</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h3>TC-TECH-05: Production Reverse Proxy Trust &amp; Header Spoofing</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Role:</strong> DevOps / Security Engineer</li>
<li><strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Staging / Production deployment configuration inspection.</li>
<li><strong>Execution:</strong><ol>
<li>Inspect <code>frontend/lib/rateLimit.ts</code>.</li>
<li>Confirm the auto-trust bug was remediated: <code>TRUST_PROXY</code> must be explicitly configured as <code>true</code> <strong>only</strong> when deployed behind an authentic reverse proxy (Cloudflare, AWS ALB, Nginx).</li>
<li>Send request with spoofed <code>X-Forwarded-For: 1.1.1.1</code> to standalone container.</li>
</ol>
</li>
<li><strong>Expected Results:</strong><ul>
<li>Standalone server ignores untrusted <code>X-Forwarded-For</code> header and extracts the true client IP from the connection socket.</li>
<li>When deployed to production behind reverse proxy, setting <code>TRUST_PROXY=true</code> extracts the authentic client IP.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><strong>Status:</strong> <strong>FIXED + UNVERIFIED IN PROD</strong> (Code fixed; live proof requires deployment behind production reverse-proxy).</li>
